  "sn22.57:18.1": "The verb “examine” (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>upaparikkhati</i>) is frequently used for someone who has learned the teachings, then internally reflects on their meaning. ",
  "sn22.57:18.2": "These three, along with the aggregates, are the major wisdom topics, mentioned together also at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn115/en/sujato#3.3'>MN 115:3.3</a>. More commonly, the aggregates, sense fields, and elements are mentioned as a summary of the Buddha’s wisdom teachings (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn8.12/en/sujato#3.2'>SN 8.12:3.2</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn35.31/en/sujato#1.21'>SN 35.31:1.21</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thig5.8/en/sujato#2.2'>Thig 5.8:2.2</a>, etc.). ",
